// A Flickable's column of repeated rows that wrap, each a layout whose wrapping text comes first and
// whose other cells are conditional. A plain layout info measures them at their preferred width, one
// line each; the Flickable's content is as tall as they are laid out, at the width it gives them.
export component TestCase inherits Window {
    width: 100px;
    height: 100px;
    property <string> words: "one two three four five six seven eight nine ten eleven twelve thirteen";
    out property <length> content: scroll.viewport-height;
    out property <length> column-height: column.height;
    out property <length> last-end: last.absolute-position.y + last.height;
    out property <length> first-height: first.height;
    in-out property <bool> asking;
    scroll := Flickable {
        viewport-width: self.width;
        VerticalLayout {
            TouchArea {
                column := VerticalLayout {
                    spacing: 16px;
                    alignment: start;
                    if root.asking: Rectangle { height: 10px; }
                    for n[i] in 6: VerticalLayout {
                        Text { wrap: word-wrap; text: root.words; font-size: 10px; }
                        if n == 100: Rectangle { height: 20px; }
                    }
                    first := Text { wrap: word-wrap; text: root.words; font-size: 10px; }
                    last := Rectangle { height: 5px; }
                }
            }
        }
    }
    out property <bool> test: root.content == root.last-end && root.column-height == root.last-end
        && root.first-height > 12px;
}

/*
```rust
let instance = TestCase::new().unwrap();
assert_eq!((instance.get_content(), instance.get_column_height()), (instance.get_last_end(), instance.get_last_end()));
assert!(instance.get_test());
instance.set_asking(true);
assert_eq!((instance.get_content(), instance.get_column_height()), (instance.get_last_end(), instance.get_last_end()));
```
*/
